{
  "description": "The rData example of records/get shows only some record types, so its shape misses most of the members Technitium writes. WriteRecordAsJson in DnsServerCore/WebServiceZonesApi.cs (v15.5.0) writes rData by record type: every type it handles gets its members here, all optional because none is written for every type. Two members change type by record type: flags is a string for DNSKEY, NSEC3, NSEC3PARAM and NAPTR records and a number for CAA records, and protocol is a number for DNSKEY records and a string for FWD records. proxyPassword of FWD records is a secret. dataType and data are written for record data the server could not read as its type; APP records use data too. Confirmed with strict response validation of records/get for whole zones against a Technitium 15.5.0 container on 2026-11-01: a Primary zone with each record type records/add creates (including APL, ZONEMD and an unknown type added as raw record data), zones signed with NSEC and NSEC3, and a conditional forwarder zone with an HTTP proxy. APP and ALIAS records, dnsKeyStateActiveBy and the fallback members come from the source only.",
